findings.message:
According to https://github.com/rust-lang/libs-team/issues/667#issuecomment-3403074426 the API that was accepted involves checking `index` in builds that contain overflow checking (debug mode or `-C overflow-checks`). I tested this and it did not panic:

```rust
#![feature(get_set_bit)]
fn main() {
    println!("{}", 0i32.bit(40));
}
```

whereas this does panic:

```rust
#![allow(arithmetic_overflow)]
fn main() {
    let index = 40;
    println!("{}", 0i32 & (1 as i32) << index != (0 as i32));
}
```

I think this attribute does the thing:

https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/blob/5f9dd05862d2e4bceb3be1031b6c936e35671501/library/core/src/num/int_macros.rs#L3289
